  "metric_interpretations": {
    "mean_absolute_error": "Mean Absolute Error (MAE): Measures the average absolute discrepancy between predicted and true sensory ratings on the original 10-point scale. Unlike squared metrics, MAE treats all error magnitudes proportionally without over-penalizing outliers.",
    "mean_squared_error": "Mean Squared Error (MSE): Averages the squared differences between predicted and actual values. Due to quadratic squaring, MSE heavily penalizes larger errors (e.g. predicting 4 for an 8).",
    "root_mean_squared_error": "Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE): The square root of MSE, returning error penalties to the original sensory rating units. A larger gap between RMSE and MAE indicates higher variance and larger residual outliers.",
    "r2_score": "Coefficient of Determination (R\u00b2): The proportion of total variance in sensory quality ratings accounted for by the 11 physicochemical predictors relative to a baseline mean predictor. Values range up to 1.0; a negative R\u00b2 indicates worse performance than predicting the training target mean.",
    "explained_variance_score": "Explained Variance: Measures the proportion to which the model accounts for the variation of the target variable, independent of mean systematic offset/bias."
  },
