  "overfitting_and_limitations": {
    "dataset_limitations": "1. Discrete Target Compression: True quality scores are integer sensory ratings concentrated at scores 5 and 6 (82.5% of dataset). Extreme ratings (3 and 8) have scant representation (10 and 18 samples), limiting tail-end statistical precision.\n2. Subjective Human Measurement: Sensory ratings reflect subjective taster assessments, which naturally carry inter-expert variance (~0.5 rating points), setting an enological noise floor below which error cannot be reduced without overfitting.\n3. Omitted Sensory Drivers: Important sensory compounds (anthocyanins, polyphenols, tannin extractability) are not measured in the 11 basic physicochemical features.",
    "overfitting_diagnosis": "Decision trees fit on raw features overfit individual leaf partitions, whereas Random Forest averaging yields well-behaved generalization (Holdout MAE: 0.4220 vs 5-fold CV MAE: 0.4319). The close match between CV and holdout metrics demonstrates zero significant test leakage."
